## 1. Java String Escaping in JavaScript — `dom` Option (DataTables)

### Problem
When embedding JavaScript code inside Java string concatenation, the DataTables `dom` option caused multiple compile errors:

```
- Syntax error on token "container", delete this token
- The target type of this expression must be a functional interface
- Syntax error on tokens, delete these tokens
```

### Root Cause
Using `\'` (invalid Java escape) inside Java string literals when building multi-line JS `dom` strings.

### Solution
Write `dom` as JS concatenation with proper Java string wrapping. Use backtick template literals inside `initComplete` for HTML injection to avoid quote conflicts:

```java
// ✅ Correct: JS concat inside Java string
+ "    dom:\r\n"
+ "      '<\"container-fluid small mb-1\"'  +\r\n"
+ "      '<\"d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center\"'  +\r\n"
+ "        '<\"me-3 custom-search-S\">' +\r\n"
+ "      '>t',\r\n"
+ "    initComplete: function () {\r\n"
+ "      $('.custom-search-S').html(`\r\n"
+ "        <div class=\"input-group input-group-sm\">\r\n"
+ "          <input type=\"search\" id=\"customSearch_S\">\r\n"
+ "        </div>\r\n"
+ "      `);\r\n"
```

### Key Rule
- Outer quotes: Java `"..."` 
- Inner JS single quotes: `'...'` — no escaping needed
- HTML attributes inside backtick template literals: `\"...\"` (escaped double quotes)

