## 2. DataTables Custom Search with `scrollY` — Input Binding Bug

### Problem
Custom keyword search input had no effect on table filtering when `scrollY` was set.

### Root Cause
Using DataTables built-in `f` (filter) slot in `dom` combined with `scrollY` causes the search input event binding to break — the input is re-rendered but the event listener is lost.

### Solution
Remove `f` from `dom`, render a custom search input manually inside `initComplete`, and register a custom filter function via `$.fn.dataTable.ext.search.push()`:

```javascript
// Register custom filter (scoped to specific table by nTable.id)
$.fn.dataTable.ext.search.push(function (settings, data, dataIndex) {
    if (settings.nTable.id !== 'tblSummary') return true;
    const val = $searchInput.val() || '';
    const isOr = $('#orMode_S').is(':checked');
    const keywords = val.toLowerCase().split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean);
    const rowText = data.join(' ').toLowerCase();
    if (keywords.length === 0) return true;
    return isOr
        ? keywords.some(k => rowText.includes(k))
        : keywords.every(k => rowText.includes(k));
});
```

### Key Points
- Always initialize `$.fn.dataTable.ext.search = []` before table init to prevent stale filter accumulation across refreshes
- Scope filters by `settings.nTable.id` when multiple DataTables exist on the same page
- OR/AND mode toggle is trivial with this pattern

