## 4. Passing Multiple Parameters via a Single Hidden Input (Pipe-Delimited)

### Problem
The `do_detail()` JS function only has 4 parameters (`mode`, `pid`, `symptom`, `range`). For the WIP detail feature, we needed to pass both `lcdType` AND `wipLocation` through the `symptom` slot.

### Solution
Combine both values with a pipe delimiter in the `symptom` argument, then parse on the Servlet side:

**Date_Servlet (building the link):**
```java
// lcdtype mode: "12|Good LCD" — lcdType pipe wipLocation
title = "do_detail('lcdtype','WIP','" + vt.getLcdType() + "|Good LCD','')";
```

**Detail Servlet (parsing):**
```java
String rawSymptom = request.getParameter("Symptom");
if (rawSymptom.contains("|")) {
    String[] parts = rawSymptom.split("\\|", 2);
    LcdType     = parts[0];   // "12"
    WipLocation = parts[1];   // "Good LCD"
} else {
    LcdType = rawSymptom;     // normal case (no WIP location filter)
}
param.put("symptom", WipLocation);
```

**Beans (filtering):**
```java
if (Type.equalsIgnoreCase("WIP") && !WipLocation.isEmpty()) {
    conds.add("A.WIP_LOCATION = '" + WipLocation + "' \r\n");
}
```

### Why This Works
- `bydate` mode: `Symptom` = WipLocation directly (e.g. `"Good LCD"`)
- `lcdtype` mode: `Symptom` = `"lcdType|WipLocation"` (e.g. `"12|Good LCD"`)
- Empty `WipLocation` = no extra filter, shows all WIP records (original behavior preserved)

