## 6. HTML `title` Attribute as Zero-Cost Tooltip on Table Links

### Problem
Table links (`do_detail()` calls) had no visual indication of what data they would load on hover.

### Solution
Add the `title` attribute to every anchor tag — the browser renders it as a native tooltip with zero additional code:

```java
// Before
as = "<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" class='ba' onClick=\"" + title + "\">";

// After — add title= with the same JS call string
as = "<a href=\"javascript:void(0)\" class='ba' title=\"" + title + "\" onClick=\"" + title + "\">";
```

**Result on hover:**
```
do_detail('bydate','WIP','RMA Wait','Monthly,2026,3')
```

### Notes
- 40 link instances updated in a single string replacement pass
- No CSS, no JS, no libraries required
- Displays the exact function call — helpful for debugging as well as UX

