## 7. WIP Location Drill-Down via `LAST_SYMPTOM` + `WIP_LOCATION` Columns

### Architecture
WIP units are classified in SQL using `LAST_PROCESS`-based CASE logic:

```sql
CASE
    WHEN LAST_PROCESS IN (89000,87900,80121,...) THEN NULL  -- not WIP
    WHEN LAST_PROCESS IN (80100,80110,80112,...) THEN 'LCM'
    WHEN LAST_PROCESS = 80120 AND LAST_DEFECT_TYPE = 'ALLGOOD' THEN 'LCM Storage (AllGood)'
    WHEN LAST_PROCESS = 80120 AND LAST_DEFECT_TYPE = 'RMA'     THEN 'LCM Storage (RMA)'
    WHEN LAST_PROCESS = 80128                                   THEN 'Frame Recycle'
    WHEN LAST_PROCESS IN (80117,86900,87000)                    THEN 'Line Reject'
    WHEN LAST_PROCESS = 87100                                   THEN 'RMA Wait'
    WHEN LAST_PROCESS IN (81000,81100,82000,...)                THEN 'Good LCD'
    ELSE 'Others'
END AS WIP_LOCATION
```

### WIP Definition
WIP includes **both**:
1. Units that completed 80117 inspection but final disposition is not yet confirmed
2. Units currently still in progress through 80117 inspection

### Data Flow
```
Line(87000) Fail → LCM(80117) Re-inspection
→ Pass  : AllGood / MnM Polishing Good
→ Fail  : OEM RMA / R2 RMA / R2 / BER Scrap / Inven Out  
→ Pending: WIP (classified by Last Process location)
```

